.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-FTS 1 "2026-10-03" "ShardPost 0.51.0" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-fts \- layouts of the full-text index: the layout 3 mark, the dictionary filter mark, the mark of online runs, the accounts with layout 3, the layout record and the key counts of an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl fts layout3 status
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts layout3 enable \-pods
.I n
.RB [ \-force ]
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts layout3 disable
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts dictfilter status
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts dictfilter enable \-pods
.I n
.RB [ \-force ]
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts dictfilter disable
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts online status
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts online enable \-pods
.I n
.RB [ \-force ]
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts online disable
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts layout3 list
.RB [ \-verify ]
.RB [ \-after
.IR account ]
.RB [ \-limit
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-json ]
.br
.B shardpostctl fts layout show
.RB [ \-json ]
.I account
.br
.B shardpostctl fts layout clear
.RB [ \-json ]
.I account
.br
.B shardpostctl fts stats
.RB [ \-exact ]
.RB [ \-parallel
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-classes ]
.RB [ \-json ]
.I account
.SH DESCRIPTION
The full-text index of an account has one of two object layouts.
Layout 2 is the fixed set of objects of every version before 0.45.0
(posting lists in
.BR fts/<nn> ,
the substring dictionary in 256 objects
.BR ftst/<nnn> ,
the header texts in
.BR ftsh/<nn> );
a delivery writes nearly all of them. Layout 3 keeps the same data in an
index generation of S posting, D dictionary and H header objects
.RB ( ftx/<gen>/p<i> ,
.BR d<j> ,
.BR h<k> )
whose counts follow the size of the account; a delivery into a small
account writes a handful of objects. The layout record in the account's
id map names the current generation, a conversion in progress and the
sources a conversion has not removed yet. Searches give the same
results in both layouts.
.PP
Servers before 0.45.0 cannot read layout 3. A cluster mark therefore
allows it: without the mark no layout 3 index is created, whatever
.I fts.layout
says (its default is 3 since 0.46.0, so the mark alone switches every
server that does not set
.IR "fts.layout: 2" ),
and
.B fts_layout
jobs refuse to convert to it. The mark is read whenever an index is
created. Every server since 0.45.0 registers itself at startup and then
every minute
.RB ( servers/<instance>
in the admin store), also without jobs or an admin listener; since
0.47.0 the push worker, scrubs and backfills register as well, each with
its role, and every process records its orderly end. A registration seen
within three minutes and not ended is fresh, one not renewed for 24
hours is deleted (by the expiry worker of the job system, and by status
and enable).
.PP
Conversions are
.B fts_layout
jobs, see
.BR shardpostctl-job (1);
between import batches the import reshard endpoint reshards under the
import session, see
.BR shardpostctl-migrate (1).
.SS fts layout3 status
Shows whether the mark is set (when, by whom, for how many pods, whether
forced) and every registration with its role, version, capabilities,
last heartbeat and freshness. With
.I admin.kv_index
other than
.B read
it lists the admin namespace. Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS fts layout3 enable
Sets the mark when exactly
.I n
fresh registrations of servers report the capability
.BR fts_layout3 .
Only servers count (role
.BR serve ,
or no role: a registration before 0.47.0); the push worker, scrubs and
backfills do not. Servers before 0.45.0 do not register, so the number
of pods running now is the check:
.B \-pods
is required. A pod that crashed less than three minutes ago leaves its
fresh record (one that ended in order does not), so the check sees one
record too many: wait three minutes, check
.BR status ,
then enable. Enable only after a rollout has completed: a server before
0.47.0 counts the registrations of the push worker, scrubs and
backfills as servers. The refusal names the instances and when they were seen.
.B \-force
skips the check; the audit log and the mark record it. Role:
.BR repair .
.SS fts layout3 disable
Removes the mark, waits five seconds (a server that read the mark just
before finishes creating its index) and lists the accounts that still
have a layout 3 index. While there are any, a downgrade to a version
before 0.45.0 is not possible: convert them back first with
.BR "shardpostctl plan \-all \-layout 2 fts_layout" .
Role:
.BR repair .
.SS fts dictfilter status
Shows whether the cluster mark of the dictionary filter
.RB ( fts/dictfilter ,
since 0.50.0) is set, with the registrations as
.BR "layout3 status" .
The mark allows index generations that a version before 0.50.0 must
not search: with the identifier filter of the substring dictionary
.RI ( "fts.dict_filter: ids" :
a body word with letters and digits of at least
.I fts.dict_id_min_runes
characters has one start entry instead of a key per trigram, so it is
found as a whole word and by its start, not by a part from its inside)
and with the text preparation without the signature and trace fields of
attached headers
.RI ( "fts.attached_headers: nosig" ).
Without the mark new generations get neither, whatever the
configuration says; existing ones change with
.B fts_layout
(the filter, see
.BR shardpostctl-job (1))
or
.B fts_rebuild
(the text preparation). Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS fts dictfilter enable
Sets the mark when exactly
.I n
fresh registrations of servers report the capability
.BR fts_dict_filter ;
otherwise as
.BR "layout3 enable" .
Role:
.BR repair .
.SS fts dictfilter disable
Removes the mark, waits five seconds, then lists the accounts whose
entry in the presence index says that a generation of theirs, current
or under way, has the filter or the text preparation
.B nosig
(set before such a generation is created, cleared after the account
switched to one without, kept in step by the scrub; an entry that
cannot be read is listed as well). It reads the presence index only, as
.B "layout3 disable"
does. While there
are any, a downgrade to a version before 0.50.0 is not possible: convert
them with
.B "fts_layout \-dict\-filter none"
and rebuild those with
.B nosig
with
.BR fts_rebuild ,
under settings that ask for neither. Role:
.BR repair .
.SS fts online status
Shows whether the cluster mark of online runs
.RB ( fts/online ,
since 0.51.0) is set, with the registrations as
.BR "layout3 status" .
The mark allows
.B fts_layout
and
.B fts_rebuild
to run without the account lock: the target generation is built beside
the current one while deliveries, logins and sessions go on; writers
record what they index meanwhile, the run catches it up and switches in
one compare-and-swap. A server before 0.51.0 does not record and waits
at the run's freeze (a temporary failure after
.IR fts.frozen_wait_seconds ),
so the mark needs every server to know it. Without the mark every run
is offline under the account lock, as before 0.51.0. Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS fts online enable
Sets the mark when exactly
.I n
fresh registrations of servers report the capability
.BR fts_online_build ;
otherwise as
.BR "layout3 enable" .
Plans with
.B \-online
are allowed from then on, and with
.I "fts.online_build: auto"
also plans without it (the reshards of the
.B fts_due
worker included). Role:
.BR repair .
.SS fts online disable
Removes the mark: new plans run offline, a plan with
.B \-online
is refused, a planned online job that has not started ends without a change (result mark_off; the fts_due worker plans it again, offline). Runs that
started finish; before a downgrade to a version before 0.51.0 wait until
no account shows
.B next_online
in
.B "fts layout show"
(or clear it with
.BR "fts layout clear" ).
Role:
.BR repair .
.SS fts layout3 list
Lists the presence index of the accounts with a layout 3 index (or a
conversion to it), a page at a time, with the time each was entered.
With
.B \-verify
each account's layout record is read (its shape shows
.BI "dict_filter ids/" n
and
.B attached_headers nosig
for a generation that has them), an entry whose account has no
layout 3 index is marked
.BR MISMATCH ,
and the largest number of dictionary objects D on the page is printed
with its account: before a way back to a version before 0.49.0,
.I fts.shards_max
must be at least the largest D of all pages (see
.BR shardpostctl-job (1),
.BR fts_layout ).
Export the list before an emergency downgrade. Role:
.B diagnose
with the scope of all accounts.
.SS fts layout show
Prints the layout record of an account: the current generation (layout
2 without a record) with its object counts, its identifier filter
.RB ( "dict_filter ids/25" )
and its text preparation
.RB ( "attached_headers nosig" )
when it has them, a conversion in progress
.RB ( next ,
the token of its run and, for an import reshard, its last heartbeat;
.B "next_online yes, mode copy"
or
.B reindex
for an online run, since 0.51.0) and
sources not removed yet
.RB ( old ,
each with the token of the run that left it and, for an import
reshard, its last heartbeat).
Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SS fts layout clear
Removes the conversion in progress of an account when its run has
ended: a job that does not run any more, or an import reshard whose
heartbeat is older than 90 seconds. Its freeze is lifted (only the
freeze of exactly that run) and its target objects are deleted; a
conversion whose run still works is left alone. Sources a run left
behind after its switch (it stopped before deleting them) are deleted
the same way when that run has ended. For an online run its records in
the id map go as well. Deliveries into an
account with a stale conversion fail temporarily after
.I fts.frozen_wait_seconds
until it is cleared; the job itself, a job or import that takes the
account lock and the jobs scrub clear it as well. Role:
.BR repair .
.SS fts stats
Prints the key counts of an account's index: its shape (with the
identifier filter and the text preparation), the documents,
the terms (posting keys) and dictionary keys, in total and per message,
and the mean number of dictionary keys per dictionary object. Without
options it reads the counters
.B !n
and
.B !dn
of the posting objects and the document count of a layout 3 index: S + 1
reads, no lock. There are no counters per dictionary or header object,
and a layout 2 index has none at all; use
.BR \-exact .
.PP
.B \-exact
counts the keys of every object page by page (librados has no key
count, and the client library cannot read keys without their values):
about one read per thousand keys, 12 000 reads for an account with 12
million index keys, alongside the deliveries, so the counts are only
roughly consistent. The values come along, so it transfers about the
account's whole index omap, posting lists and header texts included
(close to a gigabyte for the largest account on croessner). It runs
.B \-parallel
objects at a time (one by default, two for a test account) and ends
with the 5 minute write timeout of the admin
listener; raise
.B \-timeout
of
.BR shardpostctl (1)
for a large account.
.PP
.B \-classes
also counts the terms by field, class (letters, digits, mixed, other)
and length, and projects the dictionary keys for every identifier bound
n from 13 to 40: what the dictionary would hold if every body term with
letters and digits of at least n runes had one key instead of one per
trigram. It reads the terms of the posting objects and is allowed only
for the test accounts that
.I fts.stats_test_accounts
of the server names (for example the bench accounts and a test account
filled with
.BR shardpost-load );
for any other account it is refused (exit status 77). The output never
contains a term, on any account. Role:
.BR diagnose .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-pods " n"
.BR enable :
the number of servers running now (required).
.TP
.B \-force
.BR enable :
set the mark without the registrations check.
.TP
.B \-verify
.BR list :
read each account's layout record.
.TP
.BI \-after " account"
.BR list :
continue after this account (printed as
.B more:
at the end of a full page).
.TP
.BI \-limit " n"
.BR list :
accounts per page, 1 to 10000 (100).
.TP
.B \-exact
.BR stats :
count the keys of every object instead of reading the counters.
.TP
.BI \-parallel " n"
.BR "stats \-exact" :
objects counted at the same time, 1 to 16 (default 1, for a test
account 2).
.TP
.B \-classes
.BR stats :
classify the terms and project the identifier bounds (test accounts
only).
.TP
.B \-json
Print the answer as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
After the rollout of 0.45.0 to all three pods, wait three minutes, check
the registrations and allow layout 3:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl fts layout3 status
shardpostctl fts layout3 enable -pods 3
.RE
.fi
.PP
From then on new accounts get layout 3 (before 0.46.0, or with an
explicit
.IR "fts.layout: 2" ,
set
.I fts.layout: 3
in the configuration first). Convert existing accounts, for example in
a batch with small parallelism:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan -all -layout 3 fts_layout
.RE
.fi
.PP
A delivery keeps failing temporarily for one account; look for a
conversion whose run died and clear it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl fts layout show user@example.org
shardpostctl fts layout clear user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
Going back to a release before 0.45.0: set
.I fts.layout: 2
explicitly (the default is 3),
convert every account back, remove the mark (exit status 0 only when no
account has layout 3 any more), then roll the image back:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl plan -all -layout 2 fts_layout
shardpostctl fts layout3 disable
.RE
.fi
.PP
After the rollout of 0.50.0 to all three pods and the overlay with
.IR "fts.dict_filter: ids" ,
.I fts.dict_id_min_runes: 25
and
.IR "fts.attached_headers: nosig" ,
allow the dictionary filter, rebuild the test account and check its
generation and key counts, then the other accounts at a quiet time:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl fts dictfilter status
shardpostctl fts dictfilter enable -pods 3
shardpostctl plan fts_rebuild rbdpoc2@exampleserver.de
shardpostctl fts layout show rbdpoc2@exampleserver.de
shardpostctl fts stats rbdpoc2@exampleserver.de
shardpostctl plan -all fts_rebuild
.RE
.fi
.PP
Way back: with
.I fts.dict_filter: none
and
.I fts.attached_headers: all
in the configuration, find the accounts, rebuild those with
.BR nosig ,
convert the others, then remove the mark (exit status 0 only when no
generation has either property any more):
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl fts layout3 list -verify
shardpostctl plan fts_rebuild user@example.org
shardpostctl plan -all -due-only fts_layout
shardpostctl fts dictfilter disable
.RE
.fi
.PP
After the rollout of 0.51.0 to all three pods, allow online runs and
rebuild an account without locking it (deliveries and sessions go on):
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl fts online status
shardpostctl fts online enable -pods 3
shardpostctl plan -online fts_rebuild rbdpoc2@exampleserver.de
shardpostctl fts layout show rbdpoc2@exampleserver.de
.RE
.fi
.PP
How many dictionary keys per message does an account have, and how full
are its posting objects (counters only)?
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl fts stats user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
Count every object of a large account exactly, four at a time:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl -timeout 15m fts stats -exact -parallel 4 user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
Measure a test account filled with the identifier corpus: classes and
the projection per identifier bound:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl fts stats -classes rbdpoc2@exampleserver.de
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 64
Wrong arguments (for
.BR enable :
no
.BR \-pods ).
.TP
.B 65
.B enable
(each mark): the registrations do not show exactly
.I n
fresh servers with the capability of the mark;
.BR "layout3 disable" :
the mark is removed, but accounts still have layout 3;
.BR "dictfilter disable" :
the mark is removed, but generations still have the dictionary filter
or the text preparation
.BR nosig .
.TP
.B 67
No such account.
.TP
.B 70
An unexpected answer from the server.
.TP
.B 75
The server cannot be reached, or it has no layout administration.
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role
.B diagnose
(status, list, show, stats) or
.B repair
(enable, disable, clear), or the scope of all accounts (list);
.BR "stats \-classes" :
the account is not a test account of
.IR fts.stats_test_accounts .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-job (1),
.BR shardpostctl-migrate (1),
.BR shardpost-scrub (1)
